# patch: 006-account-banner-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic trees keep using
#         006-account-banner.patch, which is unchanged.
# version: authored against 2.1.260
# depends: none (the 004 multi-account half is deliberately NOT carried over --
#          004 is disabled by operator decision, so the useSwarmBanner hunk that
#          depended on __multiAccount is omitted here rather than shipped dead.)
# description: getVersionSuffix() returns ' [claudiverse]' so every version
#              readout is identifiably patched. This is the build's canary.
#
# VERSION-STRING-INDEPENDENT BY CONSTRUCTION (unchanged rationale): the hunk
# edits the one-line BODY of getVersionSuffix rather than any template literal
# embedding VERSION/BUILD_TIME/GIT_SHA, so a release bump does not by itself
# invalidate it.
#
# WHERE IT MOVED: _preamble.js DOES NOT EXIST on a chunked tree (there is no
# shared runtime preamble to carve off). getVersionSuffix survives as a tiny
# standalone chunk that the CLI entry imports directly.
#
# 🔴 THE FILE PATH ITSELF IS VERSION-VARYING. The chunk is emitted as
#   _unmatched/0003_Px.js on 2.1.260 and _unmatched/0003_dH.js on 2.1.259
#   (MEASURED on both trees): the 0003 index is stable but the suffix is the
#   chunk's minified export name. A path is not something `git apply` can
#   fuzzy-match, so this patch is version-locked at the FILENAME level and a
#   bump requires re-pointing it. Nothing in the hunk mitigates that; it is
#   stated rather than hidden.
#   What IS anchored: the retained context line `}.BUILD_REF_NAME,` is a
#   build-CONSTANT key (not a build-varying value) and was verified UNIQUE
#   across the whole 2.1.260 tree, so within the right file the hunk cannot
#   land anywhere else. The added line introduces no identifier at all.
#
# ============================================================================
# RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-07 — RE-CONTEXTED TO 2.1.263
# ============================================================================
# STATUS: 🔴 VERSION-LOCKED, AND STRUCTURALLY UNFIXABLE AS A GIT PATCH.
#         Applies to 2.1.263 (verified); FAILS on 2.1.260 (verified).
#
# WHAT BLOCKS IT — THE FILENAME, not the hunk:
#   The target is the deobfuscator's unmatched-chunk bucket, and the FILE NAME
#   itself embeds the minified export:
#       2.1.260:  _unmatched/0003_Px.js
#       2.1.263:  _unmatched/0003_$x.js
#   `git apply` matches paths LITERALLY — there is no path-glob, no fuzz, no
#   rename detection that helps here. The hunk body is already as stable as it
#   can be (context trimmed to `) {` and `}`, both byte-identical), but the
#   `diff --git` / `---` / `+++` lines can only name ONE path. So the failure
#   happens before context is ever consulted, and no amount of anchoring
#   inside the hunk can fix it.
#
# THE CONTENT ANCHOR THAT *WOULD* WORK (if the tool could use one):
#   `BUILD_REF_NAME` occurs in EXACTLY ONE file in each tree (verified by
#   grep -rl in both) — a perfect content-addressed landmark. The ordinal
#   prefix `0003_` is also stable across both. Either would locate this file
#   unambiguously, but neither is expressible in a git patch header.
#
# ⛔ WHAT WOULD UNBLOCK IT, in order of preference:
#   1. An anchor rule naming this export (it is the build-ref/version-banner
#      getter). The file would become `_unmatched/0003_<stableName>.js` and
#      this patch would go version-independent for free.
#   2. Have the deobfuscator name unmatched chunks by ORDINAL ONLY
#      (`0003.js`), which is already stable, instead of ordinal+minified name.
#   3. Apply this one edit with a content-addressed tool (sed/python keyed on
#      BUILD_REF_NAME) rather than as a git patch.
#
# The hunk itself introduces NO minified name on the added line — the change
# is a bare string literal return value.
#
diff --git a/_unmatched/0003_$x.js b/_unmatched/0003_$x.js
index 3097700..ecd6b51 100644
--- a/_unmatched/0003_$x.js
+++ b/_unmatched/0003_$x.js
@@ -22,3 +22,3 @@ function $x(
 ) {
-    return '';
+    return ' [claudiverse]';
 }
